1
00:00:00,085 --> 00:00:03,195
What if Earth spun faster,
and couldn't stop?

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,800
You are standing
on the equator,

3
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,320
and you are going
to watch what happens,

4
00:00:08,325 --> 00:00:09,675
minute by minute,

5
00:00:09,675 --> 00:00:12,445
until the planet
can't take it anymore.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,145
The Earth keeps its size,

7
00:00:15,145 --> 00:00:17,485
its shape,
its air and its water.

8
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:22,020
Only the spin changes, and
it only ever gets faster.

9
00:00:22,448 --> 00:00:24,523
On screen there
is one number

10
00:00:24,523 --> 00:00:27,268
that matters:
the length of a day.

11
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:31,385
It starts at 24 hours, and
by the end it will have

12
00:00:31,385 --> 00:00:35,000
fallen to about an hour
and 24 minutes.

13
00:00:35,293 --> 00:00:38,363
Right now,
one day lasts 24 hours.

14
00:00:38,648 --> 00:00:42,003
Standing on the equator,
the ground carries

15
00:00:42,003 --> 00:00:47,438
you around at about
1,670 kilometers an hour.

16
00:00:47,653 --> 00:00:50,723
What you do feel
is a tiny push outward.

17
00:00:51,185 --> 00:00:52,440
Hang on.

18
00:00:52,545 --> 00:00:55,365
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

19
00:00:55,575 --> 00:00:57,300
Okay, back to the math.

20
00:00:57,853 --> 00:01:00,958
You weigh about a third
of a percent less

21
00:01:00,958 --> 00:01:03,878
than you would on a planet
that did not spin.

22
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,580
And the spin has only
just begun to speed up.

23
00:01:07,653 --> 00:01:09,123
Part one of eight.
